{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1783461566,"nonce":"zxr94sbzdH7d1KuBPD2o4zFlvJo=","message":"Design correction (user, 2026-07-07): unpin/repin is never instant -- page-locking is per-page kernel work (0.6-2 GB/s here), so ANY fix that re-pins at phase boundaries just moves the cost around. Comfy avoids it by never returning pinned pages to the OS mid-run: their VBAR arena persists and pages are STOLEN between consumers via priority/watermark. Our equivalent: stop cudaHostRegister-ing 142 scattered param tensors and instead pin ONCE into per-block flat buffers (the repoint=True pack primitive that ingraph training already uses), repointing params as views. Then training streaming, bounce bypass, sampling ingraph packs, and fetch all source the same persistent pinned flats; sampling boundaries become pure ledger accounting (no kernel work, no double-commit, no pinned_weight_gib=0.0 hack). Likely also eliminates the register/unregister churn behind the 'resource already mapped' collisions (763bb75). This is pin-manager-architecture work -- coordinate with da1aae5.","files":null}]}